  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For an ideal monatomic gas, the ratio of specific heat capacity at constant pressure to specific heat capacity at constant volume is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>In an adiabatic process,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant</p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
